    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d497">

                <pb facs="0460" n="344" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg344"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 939.00/520.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the American Minister to Haiti</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-08">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 8, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Dominican Government informs the American Minister at Santo Domingo that
                    Horacio Vásquez and the two Rodriguez left Porto Rico today for Cuba, bound for
                    Haiti, and that Vásquez will import through Cape Haitien 1000 rifles and 500,000
                    rounds. You will bring this informally before the Foreign Office and say that
                    this Government expects that the projected operations of this party on Haitian
                    territory subversive of Dominican peace will be effectively prevented.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
